  "id": "Compound::DB00263 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Sulfisoxazole may interact with Cyp2c9 through a shared structural similarity with other sulfonamide compounds, such as Silver Sulfadiazine and Sulfadimethoxine. These compounds are all classified as sulfonamide anti-infective agents, and they bind to Cyp2c9, indicating a potential mechanism of action involving the cytochrome P450 enzyme. The structural resemblance between Sulfisoxazole and these compounds, along with their common classification in the sulfonamide class, supports a functional link where Sulfisoxazole may act as a substrate or inhibitor of Cyp2c9. The recurring evidence of structural similarity and enzymatic binding suggests a plausible mechanism of interaction, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
